+// GPU timestamp profiler for DeferredCommandBuffer::Execute (cvar vulkan_gpu_profile).
+// A timestamp is written before every boundary command (render pass begin, dispatch,
+// barrier, copy) and the interval up to the next one is charged to that command.
+// Each submission records into one slot (query pool); a slot is reset and reused only
+// after the submission that wrote it has completed, so results are read without waiting
+// and no query in flight is ever reset. A submission recorded but never submitted keeps
+// its slot pending and the next recording reuses it.
+// Everything except Begin/End/Stamp/Retire/Shutdown is plain bookkeeping without Vulkan
+// calls (tests/vk_gpu_profile_test.cpp).
